Some tips for concealing bribes from regulatory authorities when trying to influence a public contract bidding process include:
- Making payments to entities or persons other than the decision-makers; 
- Structuring the bribe as a loan or consultancy fee;
- Splitting up large payments into smaller ones;
- Requesting services from an individual rather than an organisation; 
- Offering amenities or discounts to stakeholders that would benefit the bidding process; and
- Establishing relationships with important members of regulatory bodies beforehand in order to make it appear as though there is no “quid pro quo” involved.
